# Dispatch Signals

This Livebook sends one Signal to a PID after an Agent commit.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A Sending Agent

```elixir
defmodule DispatchGuide.Sender do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "dispatch_guide_sender"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{sent: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0)})
    plugin Jido.Plugin.Dispatch
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/dispatch"

    route "dispatch.send" do
      action %{recipient: recipient, text: text},
        name: "dispatch_guide_send",
        schema: Zoi.object(%{recipient: Zoi.pid(), text: Zoi.string()}),
        context: context do
        outbound =
          Jido.Signal.new!(
            "dispatch.delivered",
            %{text: text},
            source: "/guides/dispatch/sender"
          )

        directive =
          Jido.Plugin.Dispatch.send(
            outbound,
            {:pid, target: recipient}
          )

        {:ok, %{context.agent_state | sent: context.agent_state.sent + 1}, [directive]}
      end

      define :send_text, args: [:recipient, :text]
    end
  end
end
```

## Send After Commit

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, sender} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    Jido.default_instance(),
    DispatchGuide.Sender,
    id: "dispatch-sender"
  )

{:ok, committed} = DispatchGuide.Sender.send_text(sender, self(), "ready")

received =
  receive do
    {:signal, signal} -> signal
  after
    5_000 -> raise "Dispatched Signal did not arrive"
  end

{committed.state.sent, received.type, received.data}
```

The Agent state commits before the Plugin calls the Jido Signal PID adapter.
The Plugin also propagates trace causation from the input Signal.

A dispatch timeout is indeterminate. The adapter can finish after the timeout.
Use receiver idempotency when retry is possible. This Plugin is not a durable
outbox.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(Jido.default_instance(), sender)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Recoverable Effects](recoverable-effects.md) when delivery must survive a
crash.
